## Acceptance

- [ ] Review the interrupted changes for syntax, types, APIs, CLI behavior,
      bounded parsing, import cycles and unintended changes. Complete or
      replace incomplete refactors; preserve concurrent legitimate work.
- [ ] Resolve actual Ruff/BasedPyright findings in every included source,
      preserving public CLI behavior and existing build-safety boundaries.
      A narrowly scoped lint exception for a necessary reviewed operation
      must explain that operation; no blanket noqa, ignored file, disabled
      type check, Any/cast shortcut or weakened root configuration.
- [ ] Keep the validator small, static and standard-library based; no new
      framework, installs, downloads, kext compiler invocation or database
      generation. Default-on tests (or explicit --tests) support offline host
      tests in Python/C++/Objective-C++ under root tests/, including isolated
      host compilation. Do not execute the kext build or device-check scripts.
      Default-on Clang-Tidy needs an existing compilation database.
- [ ] Finish formatting/type work before claiming a source task is clean.
      Missing tools or skipped requested checks are limitations, not passes.
- [ ] Commit reviewed changes in focused main commits, then obtain a fresh
      full tools/validate.py --no-cache report without concurrent source
      mutation. Record the exact scope, tools, counts and commit; no stale
      per-file cache/report may stand in for the full result.
- [ ] Update this record with actual results and remove its TODO index entry
      only after the findings above are resolved. Never infer functional
      Wi-Fi, ABI correctness or panic freedom from green lint.

